ic general-election polling", "Marx's fundraising pace and cash burn raise GOP competitiveness questions but not enough to close the gap"], "rationale": "Colorado's structural Democratic lean, a unanimous Solid/Safe D rating consensus, and markets pricing Weiser near 97% all point to a comfortable Democratic win in this open-seat race. With no public polling to refine the estimate, the forecast stays near the fundamentals-based margin of roughly 12 points.", "watch": "A shift in the national midterm environment toward Republicans, or signs that Marx's fundraising is converting into a durable polling lead, could tighten the race.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Open seat: Jared Polis (D) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Colorado's governorship is open as Jared Polis is term-limited, and Attorney General Phil Weiser carries the Democratic banner against Republican nominee Victor Marx. The state's six-point Democratic lean and the absence of an incumbent penalty on either side shape the fundamentals. Every major race rater calls the contest Solid or Safe Democratic, and prediction markets on Kalshi, Polymarket, and PredictIt all price a Democratic win around 97%.\n\nNo public general-election polls are available, so the forecast leans on fundamentals and expert consensus, landing near a twelve-point Democratic margin. Marx has kept pace with Weiser in fundraising but is spending quickly, and the two have clashed over debates. Minor-party candidates, including independent Greg Lopez, appear on the ballot but are unlikely to alter the outcome materially.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9695, "margin": 12.28}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9628, "margin": 12.0}]}